cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset or the papers, please cite the repository. Version v2.0.0 refers to the repository as of 2026-09-19. A matching GitHub Release will be tagged v2.0.0."
title: "AI Hallucination Research: hallucination trial dataset, transcripts, and papers"
type: dataset
version: "v2.0.0"
date-released: "2026-09-19"
url: "https://github.com/mahashu/ai-hallucination-research"
repository-code: "https://github.com/mahashu/ai-hallucination-research"
license: CC-BY-4.0
abstract: >-
  Trial dataset, full transcripts, and papers from a research project on why
  large language models fabricate confident, false information and what
  reduces it. Gemini, ChatGPT, and Claude were tested under several prompting
  conditions, including a short intervention (IDK+COMP). Every trial was coded
  by hand for hallucination and hedging. The transcripts are AI-generated by
  design and are the object of study, not factual sources.
keywords:
  - hallucination
  - large language models
  - AI safety
  - LLM evaluation
  - dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Kowalski
    given-names: Michelle
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-4193-8482"
  - name: "Claude (Anthropic)"
  - name: "ChatGPT (OpenAI)"
  - name: "Gemini (Alphabet Inc.)"
